# **Do not edit this file.** Subclass PluginBase in the plugin file each student claimed.
"""Shared type for every plugin.

Subclass ``PluginBase``. The methods you implement live in your plugin
file (``partitioning.py``, ``leader_election.py``, and so on). The running process
is passed in as ``node``.
"""


class PluginBase:
    """What you can use on ``node`` while you fill in a plugin:

    - ``node.node_id``, ``node.nodes``, ``node.leader``, ``node.term``
    - ``node.store`` (key → bytes), ``node.log``, ``node.directory``
    - ``node.rpc(peer_id, method, request)`` — call another node
      (``"Write"``, ``"Read"``, ``"Replicate"``, ``"Elect"``, ``"Prepare"``, …).
      Pause, drop, and delay on that peer still apply.
    - ``node.reachable()``, ``node.other_nodes()``
    - Forwarded ``Write`` / ``Read`` requests carry ``hop``. Stop after 8.
    """
